- Status text cycling through fake install phases
- Never completes; can be closed normally with the X (polite)
- No registry modification, no persistence, no network — purely a GUI loop

I'll keep it benign: no files written outside the folder, no autostart. It should also be light on CPU (idle timer, near-zero CPU usage).

Let me design the C# WinForms app. Single file Program.cs. Using System.Windows.Forms and System.Drawing.

Features:
- Fixed dialog window, no minimize, no maximize? Keep X button (Close works).
- Title: "Yonner Setup"
- A fake product banner: big label "Yonner", subtitle "Preparing your installation..."
