- Progress bar: marquee style (indeterminate) — loops forever. Or a determinate bar that asymptotically crawls to 99% and never finishes. Marquee is simplest and truly "loops forever". I'll do marquee plus a percentage readout that goes up and down? Marquee is good. Maybe combine: marquee progress bar + elapsed time counter + files count that keeps incrementing — looks alive forever.

Design details:
- Timer every 120ms: update files counter (adds random 1-7), elapsed time, cycle status text every ~4 seconds from array, occasionally "retry" messages like "Taking longer than usual...", etc.
