& $csc /target:winexe /out:"...\Yonner Installer.exe" /reference:System.Windows.Forms.dll /reference:System.Drawing.dll Program.cs

Also maybe generate an icon? Could compile with a simple icon extracted... skip, default icon fine. Could add /win32icon with a generated icon — I could generate an image with experimental_image_generate and convert to .ico? Converting png→ico needs tooling; .NET can build icon? There's no easy built-in converter. Skip icon, or set form's icon from a drawn bitmap at runtime (paint a "Y"). I can draw a simple icon at runtime: create a Bitmap, draw "Y", set as form icon — nice touch, no deps.

